# Unanchored so nested build dirs are ignored too — apps/windows/target/ survives from
# the pre-workspace layout, and "/target" would only have matched the root one.
target/

# Cargo.lock IS committed: this workspace ships a binary (airclip-windows), and Rust
# convention is to lock applications so builds and `cargo audit` are reproducible.
# (Libraries omit it; airclip-core is consumed only from inside this workspace.)
# apps/ios/Generated/ is deliberately NOT ignored: ARCHITECTURE §2 checks the Swift
# bindings in so an Xcode build never has to run Rust, and CI's freshness gate diffs
# them. The xcframework stays out — it is a large binary artefact the script rebuilds.
*.xcframework
# Generated by XcodeGen from apps/ios/project.yml — never hand-edited, never committed.
# Keeping project.pbxproj out of git is what makes the spec the single source of truth
# and removes the usual merge-conflict surface.
*.xcodeproj/
xcuserdata/
DerivedData/
.DS_Store
